From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 08:45:13 +0000
Subject: soc: cix: dst: keep all characters of the parsed log fields

strscpy() keeps count - 1 characters, so the level and time fields
lost their last character. A time of 0x143 parsed as 0x14. Copy the
measured length with memcpy(). Reject a length that leaves no room
for the terminator.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
---
 drivers/soc/cix/cix_dst/blackbox/rdr_dump_core.c | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/cix/cix_dst/blackbox/rdr_dump_core.c b/drivers/soc/cix/cix_dst/blackbox/rdr_dump_core.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/cix/cix_dst/blackbox/rdr_dump_core.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/cix/cix_dst/blackbox/rdr_dump_core.c
@@ -75,14 +75,14 @@ static int parse_log_entry(const char *input, log_entry *entry)
 	log_offset = log_str - input + 7;
 	level_len = time_offset - 10 - level_offset;
 	time_len = log_offset - 9 - time_offset;
-	if (level_len > sizeof(entry->level) || time_len > sizeof(time)) {
+	if (level_len >= sizeof(entry->level) || time_len >= sizeof(time)) {
 		BB_PN("log len err, %s\n", input);
 		return -1;
 	}
 
-	strscpy(entry->level, input + level_offset, level_len);
+	memcpy(entry->level, input + level_offset, level_len);
 	entry->level[level_len] = '\0';
-	strscpy(time, input + time_offset, time_len);
+	memcpy(time, input + time_offset, time_len);
 	time[time_len] = '\0';
 	entry->log = (char *)input + log_offset;
 
-- 
